<article class="env-corollary" id="06BW">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06BW">Corollary <span data-tag="06BW">8.1.1.16</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be an inner fibration of simplicial sets. Then the induced map $\operatorname{Tw}(U): \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ is an inner fibration. If $U$ is an isofibration, then $\operatorname{Tw}(U)$ is also an isofibration. </p>
